<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net48</TargetFramework>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <BaseOutputPath>.\bin</BaseOutputPath>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    A third test project, for the same reason there is a second one: **these tests must run without
    TIA Portal.**

    What belongs here is anything that is text in and text out. That started as cell specifications
    and template expansion and now also covers SimulationTagValueParser, which turns the text of a
    tag write into a value: no controller, no portal, and the one part of the simulation code that a
    laptop can check. The criterion is the run-without-TIA one, not the subject matter.

    TiaMcpServer.Test starts a portal in [AssemblyInitialize], so every test in that assembly pays
    for one and none of them can run on a machine without a licence. Cell specifications and template
    expansion are text in and text out, so making them wait for a portal would be paying that price
    for nothing - and worse, it would mean nobody could check the patterns on a laptop.

    Why not put them in TiaMcpServer.Governance.Test, which already runs without TIA? Because that
    project holds one explicit test per safety rule, as CLAUDE.md requires, and its value comes from
    being exactly that list. Filling it with SCL template tests would make the safety tests harder to
    find, which is the one thing that project cannot afford.

    Note what this project does NOT cover: whether the generated SCL compiles. Nothing here can know
    that. Test19CellPattern in the TIA suite writes the real patterns into a real project and
    compiles them, and that is the test that says the patterns are correct. These say the text came
    out as intended, which is a different and smaller claim.

    The two entries below are repository-wide style decisions already justified in
    src/TiaMcpServer/TiaMcpServer.csproj, repeated so the same code does not pass in one project and
    fail in another.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);IDE0008</NoWarn>  <!-- var: CLAUDE.md asks for judgement the analyzer cannot make -->
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CA1861</NoWarn>   <!-- constant arrays as arguments: a hot-path concern, in test setup -->
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" Version="17.14.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="MSTest" Version="3.9.2" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\TiaMcpServer.Portable\TiaMcpServer.Portable.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Using Include="Microsoft.VisualStudio.TestTools.UnitTesting" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
